    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d270">

                <pb facs="0450" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg410"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Hunter</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 996.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 22, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit a few more
                    addresses, &amp;c, on the assassination of the late President. As this process
                    has now pretty much come to an <pb facs="0451" n="411" xml:id="pg411"/> end, the
                    probability is that you already have all the means in your power to decide upon
                    the most advisable and compendious mode of acknowledgment.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Hunter,</hi> Esq.,<hi rendition="#italic"
                            > Acting Secretary of State, Washington, D. C</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d270-a1.xml" xpointer="d270-a1"/>
